WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.690
Two savings accounts.

2
00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.250
Each starts with ten thousand pounds.

3
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.610
Each pays four per cent
a year, for ten years.

4
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.670
Account A adds its interest once a year.

5
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.800
Account B splits the four per
cent into twelve smaller pieces,

6
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.950
and adds one every month.

7
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.470
After ten years, does
Account B end up with more?

8
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.350
Or is four per cent just four per cent?

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.290
In this mission, you'll see why compound
interest earns interest on the interest,

10
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.440
multiplying by the same
factor each period.

11
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:36.560
You'll use the future value formula, with
the yearly rate split into k periods.

12
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.230
Monthly means k is twelve.

13
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.970
Your mission: work out what monthly
compounding adds to ten thousand pounds at

14
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.030
four per cent for ten years.
